body:
Intended label: `enhancement` (gh won't let this account add labels).

**Today:** the only feature-based WCS placement is the Geometry page's "Align WCS (3-2-1)" button (#187, `crates/app/src/pick/align.rs`): it reads the open operation's pick chips with fixed roles - one flat face becomes Z (outward normal), one straight edge becomes X (projected into that plane), one vertex or bore centre becomes the origin. That means:

- no role choice - a face is always Z and an edge is always X. You cannot put a bore's axis along WCS X, or stand Z on an edge;
- a cylinder's wall can only contribute its centre as the origin - its axis never aligns to anything;
- the picks land in the open operation's geometry chips, so aligning the WCS pollutes the operation's feature list.

**Expected:** a WCS-from-features pick mode where each pick carries a chosen role - Origin, X, Y or Z - over flat faces, straight edges, vertices and curved walls (cylinder patches):

- a flat face gives a plane (outward normal), a straight edge a direction, a vertex a point, a curved wall a fitted axis and centre (the axis fit from wall facets is new: `circle_of_region` fits circles only on level rings of vertical walls, there is no general axis fit today);
- any two distinct axis picks fix the orientation, the third axis is derived right-handed by cross product; the Origin pick is optional, and without it the origin falls on a sensible feature point;
- degenerate picks refuse by name: two axis picks too near parallel to separate, a doubled role, gone features say re-pick, and the #366 winding refusals carry over.

**Done means:** an armed "Set WCS from features" pick mode following the Setups page's "Lay on a plane" pattern (#330: `crates/ui/src/plane_pick.rs` + `setup_plane_pick.rs`): arm, viewport clicks land in the draft (never in operation chips), and a live-gated Apply queues the existing `CommandKind::SetWcs` - one undo step, no new command kind. Tests pin the role table, every named refusal, and a cylinder-axis fit on a bore turned off-axis. The existing "Align WCS (3-2-1)" button stays as it is.

Provenance: user-assigned datum alignment as in common fixture practice; all math stays our own.
